  "rebuild": "2026-10-27 (Swarm audit job 388b71cb fixes, then a pre-deployment review): expired seed block keeps its public secret and re-arms; commitment re-arms bounded (2 per epoch, shared by epochs waiting behind it) with a cooldown from the current seed block; acceptance names the commitment it replaces; chosen-skin freeze from the natural seed block; 32 hashes above every anchor refused; storage repacked for gas (signer + sale flags + freeStartAt + eligibleWalletCount in one slot, reveal progress + re-arm in one slot, 8 random epochs per word); rearmBlock, rearmFromEpoch, revealedSecrets, paidMinted views removed; same solc 0.8.38 payload and settings. 2026-10-28 (Swarm audit job d726b1cd): an expiry re-arm moves only its own epoch; commitment re-arms counted from the last two commitment blocks (an expiry never counts, nor a commitment set before the epoch closed); reveal-commitment acceptance valid at most 1 hour. Owner 2026-10-28: payment to an immutable paymentRecipient set at deployment (the treasury Safe) instead of the burn address; default supply 1,688 (1,068/218/218/68/68/48); TestUSD added for the Sepolia rehearsal; ERC-2981 royalty 2.5% to the treasury; gas review: free claims as a bitmap keyed by free-list index, paid route verifies only the rebuilt PaidAuthorization, totalSupply check removed; 2026-10-28 (Swarm audit job b0b1d96a): the reveal-commitment acceptance signs a recent block number and hash instead of a deadline (valid while blockhash() knows the block); comments restate the reach of an expiry re-arm; same solc 0.8.38 payload and settings"
}
